Hollywood loves sequels even if the  audience doesn't always agree here's a  handful of would-be franchise expanders  that didn't come anywhere near  duplicating the success of their  predecessors a Christmas story - my  summer story being a Hollywood producer  has its risks but at least you won't  shoot your eye out if you make a sadly  subpar and utterly unnecessary sequel to  a beloved holiday classic oh my god I  shot my eye out you'll shoot your eye  out  our proof lies in my summer story the  long delayed follow-up to a Christmas  story originally titled it runs in the  family this 1994 release did have a  couple ties to the original like being  based on stories by Jean Shepard who  returned to provide narration but given  that the entire cast of the original was  too old to reprise their roles a whole  new set of stars had to be moved in  including Charles Grodin and Mary  Steenburgen reviews weren't entirely  unkind with the film's box office gross  which total less than 71 thousand  dollars speaks for itself Legally Blonde  after 2003's Legally Blonde - red white  and blonde Reese Witherspoon was just  about done with the character of bimbo  turned lobbyist Elle Woods but after  watching the franchise continued without  her with a successful Legally Blonde  stage musical she took the reins once  more as producer of this 2009  direct-to-dvd spin-off the most  interesting and sad thing about the  movie is the involvement of director  savage steve holland who's once proud  filmography kicked off with a John  Cusack classic better off dead here  viewers watch as else twin cousins move  into her old house and you know what it  really isn't worth talking about the  plot suffice to say that small dogs and  a life lesson in the final actor  involved Ace Ventura jr. more than a  decade after Jim Carrey acted at the Ace  Ventura franchise someone got the bright  idea to continue the series without him  by attempting to tell the story of his  look like kid who gets mixed up in  solving some pet related wrongdoings  after a senior flies the coop it's a  horrible idea for  well even one that went direct video and  it was greeted with all the commercial  and difference in critical scoring you  might expect if it arrived in the 90s  you probably would have seen it at your  favorite blockbuster alas by the late  Ott's that could only gather dust on a  loneliest DVD rack at your local Best  Buy wargames the dead code unlike a lot  of technologically driven films wargames  remains a pretty solid little action  thriller not least because it boasts the  combined talents of Matthew Broderick  Ally Sheedy Dabney Coleman and Barry  Corbin none of the above returned for  the holy lamentable war games the dead  code which tried to duplicate the teen  hacker excitement of the original by  essentially copying the plot right down  to the reintroduction of wargames senior  computer whiz Stephen Falken played here  by a new actor who didn't even appear in  the original needless to say these new  wargames had no winners Adams family  reunion seeking to reboot the Addams  Family franchise after 1991 s The Addams  Family and 1993 s The Addams Family  Values Fox decided to start it over  again as a new TV show called the new  Addams Family featuring a new cache then  who had appeared in the movies and then  the studio filmed the made-for-tv movie  Addams family reunion which was supposed  to serve as the serious pilot even  though it had yet another cast of actors  in the lead roles confused yet just be  glad you weren't Tim curry or Daryl  Hannah both of whom somehow ended up  roped into this alternately unfunny and  offensive alleged comedy unsurprisingly  neither the movie nor the show it  launched had much of a legacy the new  Addams Family exit the airwaves after a  two season run and there have been no  family reunions since Roadhouse - last  call there are definitely people in the  world that would argue that Patrick  Swayze's Roadhouse is a classic it's  hard to imagine though that many of them  would go so far as to say we needed a  sequel let alone one starring Jonathan's  check if you remember him at all it's  probably from that thing you do you know  the whiny guitar player who didn't live  Tyler well now you can have Roadhouse -  to your list or don't probably don't  check stars a Swayze's characters son a  DEA agent who ends up running his  uncle's club after a local drug kingpin  beats him half to death  if you're guessing that the kid  ultimately discovers that the kingpin is  the same bad guy who murdered his dad  the nearest step ahead of the target  audience for Roadhouse  last call maybe go a step further and  skip this one and just watch that thing  you do again  man tooth fairy - you're setting a  pretty low bar for comedy when you hired  Dwayne the rock Johnson to run around in  fairy wings but even when it's held up  against the relaxed standard set by the  original Tooth Fairy its little seen  sequel is an ordeal the rock obviously  wasn't coming back for another round so  the producers hired Larry the Cable Guy  on the assumption that like the rock he  provoked laughs simply by strapping on  fairy wings it didn't work and neither  did hiring a pig as one of Larry's  co-stars splash - splash - was Disney's  attempt to cobble together a sequel to  its hit mermaid rom-com starring Tom  Hanks and Daryl Hannah  with neither star affordable enough for  a TV movie the studio almost completely  overhauled the cast originally broadcast  as a two-part event splash - has been  all but forgotten even the reissue  fanatics at Disney haven't gotten around  to putting it out on DVD or blu-ray  National Lampoon's Christmas vacation -  cousin Eddie's Island Adventure that's a  mouthful cousin Eddie the brain hick who  drove Clark crazy and a pair of national  lampoon's vacation movies could be  fairly funny in limited doses naturally  this was all the justification the  studio needed for basing an entire  vacation movie around Eddie after Chevy  Chase in beverly d'angelo were finished  with the franchise the horribly titled  National Lampoon's Christmas vacation -  cousin Eddie's Isle adventure starts  with Eddie losing his job to a monkey  and goes downhill from there with star  Randy Quaid huffing and puffing his way  through a series of increasingly lame  pratfalls maybe the movie would have  turned out better if they just replaced  Quaid with a monkey all together  just kidding we still love you Randy and  last and equally least bachelor party to  the Last Temptation Studios cranked out  a ton of sex comedies in the 80s and  1984 his bachelor party  would have been just another one of them  if it's star Tom Hanks hadn't gone on to  superstardom later in the decade more  than 20 years later Fox tried making  lightning strike twice with bachelor  party - The Last Temptation it was a  sequel in name only they gathered up a  group of stock character types - love  for the cameras in between gratuitous  topless shots  sadly for the studio the next Hanks  doesn't seem to have been in the cast  but that doesn't mean we won't hear  about a bachelor party three in 20  - thanks for watching subscribe to our  YouTube channel to watch more videos  like the one you just saw and leave us a  comment to let us know which obscure  movie sequels should have made the list
 

